      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:proclus.homily13.budge",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁϥⲕⲁⲁⲩ ⲛⲁϥ ϩⲛⲧⲉϥ**ⲫⲩⲥⲓⲥ** ⲉⲧⲛⲁⲛⲟⲩⲥ · ⲉⲣⲉⲡⲉⲩⲟⲩⲱϣ ⲥⲱⲕ ⲙⲙⲟⲟⲩ ⲙⲙⲏⲛⲉ ⲉⲧⲣⲉϥⲙⲉⲣⲓⲧⲟⲩ ⲛϩⲟⲩⲟ ·",
      "english": "and in his good nature he set them apart to minister unto himself. And their own natural disposition drew them more and more day by day to make him love them,",
      "source": "History of Eustathius and Theopiste part 2",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lives.eustathius.budge:31-56",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲧⲁⲓ ϩⲱⲱⲥ ⲧⲉ ⲧϩⲉ ⲛⲧⲉ**ⲫⲩⲥⲓⲥ** ⲙⲡⲛⲟⲃⲉ · ⲉⲥϣⲁⲛⲏϩ ⲛⲣϫⲟⲉⲓⲥ ⲉⲡⲗⲟⲅⲓⲥⲙⲟⲥ ⲛⲧⲉⲯⲩⲭⲏ · ϣⲁⲥⲧⲁⲕⲟ ⲛⲧⲉⲯⲩⲭⲏ ⲧⲏⲣⲥ · ⲁⲩⲱ ⲡⲕⲉⲥⲱⲙⲁ ⲛⲙⲙⲁⲥ ·",
      "english": "even so is it in the case of the natural disposition of sin, which finally obtaineth the mastery over the reasoning power of the soul, and then destroyeth the whole soul itself, and the body also with it.",
